            <div purpose="slack-window" aria-hidden="true">
              <picture purpose="slack-chrome">
                <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/images/slack-chat-window-mobile-402x552.svg">
                <source media="(max-width: 991px)" srcset="/images/slack-chat-window-tablet-844x602.svg">
                <img alt="" src="/images/slack-chat-window-1044x602.svg">
              </picture>
              <span purpose="slack-section-label">Channels</span>
              <span purpose="slack-channel-label">ask fleet</span>
              <span purpose="slack-channel-title">ask fleet</span>
              <span purpose="slack-thread-title">Thread</span>
              <div purpose="slack-messages">
                <div purpose="slack-question">
                  <img purpose="slack-avatar" alt="" src="/images/avatar-slack-mike-36x36@2x.png">
                  <p purpose="slack-typing">Mike is <strong>typing...</strong></p>
                  <div purpose="slack-message-body">
                    <span purpose="slack-sender">Mike</span>
                    <p><span purpose="slack-mention">@fleet</span>&nbsp; which Macs in Engineering have an MCP server with shell access, and are any of them behind on macOS?</p>
                    <div purpose="slack-reactions">
                      <div purpose="slack-status-reaction">
                        <span purpose="slack-pending">⏳<span>1</span></span>
                        <span purpose="slack-done">✅<span>1</span></span>
                      </div>
                      <span purpose="slack-add-reaction"><img alt="" src="/images/icon-slack-add-reaction-13x13.svg"></span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div purpose="slack-first-reply">
                  <img purpose="slack-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-slack-36x36.svg">
                  <div purpose="slack-message-body">
                    <span purpose="slack-sender">Fleet <span purpose="slack-app-badge">APP</span></span>
                    <div purpose="slack-reply-text">
                      <p purpose="slack-thinking">⏳ Thinking...</p>
                      <div purpose="slack-answer">
                        <p>14 of 1,120 Engineering Macs have an MCP server with shell access. 5 of those are also behind on macOS, still on 15.7. Want me to propose a fix?</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div purpose="slack-yes">
                  <img purpose="slack-avatar" alt="" src="/images/avatar-slack-mike-36x36@2x.png">
                  <p purpose="slack-typing">Mike is <strong>typing...</strong></p>
                  <div purpose="slack-message-body">
                    <span purpose="slack-sender">Mike</span>
                    <p>Yes</p>
                    <div purpose="slack-reactions">
                      <div purpose="slack-status-reaction">
                        <span purpose="slack-pending">⏳<span>1</span></span>
                        <span purpose="slack-done">✅<span>1</span></span>
                      </div>
                      <span purpose="slack-add-reaction"><img alt="" src="/images/icon-slack-add-reaction-13x13.svg"></span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div purpose="slack-second-reply">
                  <img purpose="slack-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-slack-36x36.svg">
                  <div purpose="slack-message-body">
                    <span purpose="slack-sender">Fleet <span purpose="slack-app-badge">APP</span></span>
                    <div purpose="slack-reply-text">
                      <p purpose="slack-thinking">⏳ Thinking...</p>
                      <div purpose="slack-answer">
                        <p>Done. I’ve proposed a policy that flags MCP shell access and a macOS update deadline for those 5 Macs, <span purpose="slack-link">for your review</span>.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading" class="left-aligned">
          <h2>A safer, faster way to make changes</h2>
          <p>Fleet works natively with your team’s AI tools, like Claude, Copilot, or any AI harness. Use it to propose changes, with a human review between it and your devices.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="two-column-features">
          <div purpose="feature">
            <h5>Get AI working for you</h5>
            <p>Generate configuration profiles and DDM declarations with prompts like <em>“Block iCloud Drive on company Macs”</em>.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature">
            <h5>Chat with your Macs</h5>
            <p>See what’s patched and what’s compliant without waiting hours. Investigate CVEs and supply chain issues in seconds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

